          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The formula for the number of diagonals of a polygon with ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "n",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " sides is ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "D=\\frac{n}{2}(n-3)",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". How many sides does a polygon with 44 diagonals have?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "11 sides.",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the number of sides. With $D=44$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{n}{2}(n-3)&=44\\\\n(n-3)&=88\\\\n^2-3n-88&=0\\\\(n-11)(n+8)&=0\\\\n-11&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad n+8=0\\\\n&=11\\quad\\text{or}\\quad n=-8\\end{align*}$$\n\nA polygon cannot have a negative number of sides, so reject $n=-8$. Hence, the polygon has 11 sides.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
